From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] glx: a stereo child is declared once its window is viewable

Netgen's drawing area is a Togl child window of a Tk window. Tk creates the
child and draws it once while the top-level window is still unmapped (0.58 s
after the start in the rig), and maps the window 0.7 s later. Stereo KWin
cannot take a child of a window that is not on the screen, so the declaration
made at that first swap met the 500 ms wait of 0043 without an answer, the
presents that completed as copies took the declaration back, and the drawing
area stayed flat after the window was mapped ("stereo child 0x...: the
compositor did not take the child in 500 ms", then the problems engine's
"is shown flat"). Both GLX paths, DRI3 and the software one, now leave the
declaration of a child window to the first swap after the window is viewable
(XWindowAttributes.map_state == IsViewable, which holds only when the window
and every ancestor are mapped); a top-level window is declared as before.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
---
--- a/src/glx/dri_common.c
+++ b/src/glx/dri_common.c
@@ -377,6 +377,28 @@
    return arrived;
 }
 
+/* A child window of a window that is not on the screen yet cannot be taken by the
+ * compositor: Tk (Netgen's drawing area) and other toolkits create the GL child, draw
+ * once and map the top-level window some time later.  The declaration of such a child
+ * waits until the window is viewable: declared earlier, the compositor holds nothing
+ * to answer within the wait of glx_x11_wait_stereo_child_adopted, the presents that
+ * complete as copies take the declaration back, and the child stays flat.
+ */
+bool
+glx_x11_stereo_child_hidden(Display *dpy, Window window, int map_state)
+{
+   Window root, parent, *kids = NULL;
+   unsigned int nkids;
+
+   if (map_state == IsViewable)
+      return false;
+   if (!XQueryTree(dpy, window, &root, &parent, &kids, &nkids))
+      return false;
+   if (kids)
+      XFree(kids);
+   return parent != root && parent != None;
+}
+
 void
 glx_x11_wait_stereo_child_adopted(Display *dpy, int screen, Window window)
 {
--- a/src/glx/dri_common.h
+++ b/src/glx/dri_common.h
@@ -129,6 +129,8 @@
 glx_x11_undeclare_stereo_child(Display *dpy, Window window);
 void
 glx_x11_wait_stereo_child_adopted(Display *dpy, int screen, Window window);
+bool
+glx_x11_stereo_child_hidden(Display *dpy, Window window, int map_state);
 #endif /* GLX_DIRECT_RENDERING */
 
 #endif /* _DRI_COMMON_H */
--- a/src/glx/dri3_glx.c
+++ b/src/glx/dri3_glx.c
@@ -275,6 +275,10 @@
        attributes.width > INT_MAX / 2)
       return;
 
+   if (glx_x11_stereo_child_hidden(pdraw->base.psc->dpy, pdraw->base.xDrawable,
+                                   attributes.map_state))
+      return;
+
    const unsigned version =
       glx_x11_stereo_support_version(pdraw->base.psc->dpy, pdraw->base.psc->scr);
 
--- a/src/glx/drisw_glx.c
+++ b/src/glx/drisw_glx.c
@@ -611,6 +611,9 @@
        attributes.width <= 0 || attributes.width > INT_MAX / 2)
       return;
 
+   if (glx_x11_stereo_child_hidden(dpy, pdraw->base.xDrawable, attributes.map_state))
+      return;
+
    if (!pdraw->base.dri_drawable->stereo_view_width)
       pdraw->base.dri_drawable->stereo_view_width = attributes.width;
 
